1
00:00:01,918 --> 00:00:03,712
Lalit Singh Banra: What is your name?

2
00:00:04,629 --> 00:00:07,674
My name is Ladura Singh Haiburu.

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:08,800
Village?

4
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:10,510
The village is Keshpada.

5
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:11,386
Keshpada...

6
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:12,679
So, Ladura Babu,

7
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:18,059
What do you call body parts from head to toe

8
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:20,103
in our Ho language?

9
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:23,481
Can you tell me a little bit?

10
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:25,442
Okay, alright.

11
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:30,572
This one, which is at the top...

12
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:31,406
Yes, yes...

13
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:32,824
This is called "bōḥ-bālē" (hair).

14
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:33,575
Okay, alright.

15
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:34,701
"Bōḥ bālē" (Head hair).

16
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:40,915
Yes, it is "bōḥ" (head)

17
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:42,417
Yeah, it is "bōḥ" (head).

18
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:46,546
So now I'm coming to the front.

19
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:47,464
Hmm...hmm...

20
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:49,382
Now showing you...

21
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:50,967
It is called "muṭā" (nose).

22
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:51,885
Hmm, hmm...

23
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,595
This is called "mēḍ" (eye).

24
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:54,345
Hmm, hmm...

25
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:56,931
Yes, the one above is called "rānāpiḍ" (eyelids)...

26
00:00:56,931 --> 00:00:57,849
..called "rānāpiḍ" (eyelids)

27
00:00:57,849 --> 00:00:58,516
Hmm...hmm...

28
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:00,018
Hmm...

29
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:03,772
This is called "īñēla" (eyebrow).

30
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:04,522
Hmm...

31
00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:07,525
Hmm...this is "luṭi" (lip).

32
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:08,526
Hmm, hmm...

33
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:10,653
It's the whole "aa" (mouth).

34
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:11,571
Hmm, hmm...

35
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,947
It's "dāṭā" (teeth).

36
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:13,865
Hmm, hmm...

37
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:14,949
There are two types of teeth—

38
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:16,326
"gānaḍu-dāṭā" (internal incisors).

39
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,161
The ones inside are called "gānaḍu- dāṭā" (internal incisors)...

40
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:18,745
Okay.

41
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:19,913
..and "muli dāṭā" (front teeth).

42
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:20,580
Hmm, hmm...

43
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:25,043
Then, "lutur" (ear) is on this side.

44
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:27,420
So, this is "lutur" (ear), right?

45
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:29,005
A little down...

46
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,423
..this is called "jōa" (cheek).

47
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:31,674
"Jōa" (Cheek)...

48
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,010
This side is also called "jōa" (cheek).

49
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:34,969
This is "tāṛu" (chin).

50
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:36,846
This is called "tāṛu" (chin).

51
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:39,974
This one from here is "hōṭōḥ" (neck), neck.

52
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:41,518
"Hōṭōḥ" (Neck).

53
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,770
This is "tārān" (shoulder).

54
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:44,354
"Tārān" (Shoulder).

55
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,271
Alright.

56
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:49,400
From here goes "supu" (arm).

57
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,027
Here goes the arm.

58
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:53,571
Yes, this is where the arm is...

59
00:01:53,571 --> 00:01:55,615
..from here to here.

60
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:56,783
Yes, its called "supu" (arm).

61
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:59,035
.arm, arm, arm [it is] called.

62
00:01:59,035 --> 00:02:01,788
"Tii" (Hands)—from here to here.

63
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:02,664
"Tii" (Hands). Yeah...

64
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,165
Oh, till "jōṅa" (bone)...

65
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:06,334
Until then...Until then...

66
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:06,960
Yes.

67
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:07,794
Okay...okay.

68
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:09,546
Yes, these are "aṅguṛi" (fingers).

69
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,297
Yes, these are fingers.

70
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:13,091
This is called "sārsār" (nails).

71
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:13,925
"Sārsār".

72
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:15,885
So, they are called "sārsār"?

73
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:17,220
Yeah, they are called "sārsār".

74
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,388
"Sārsār". "Sārsār".

75
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:22,600
Do our fingers have names?...

76
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,685
..can you say more?

77
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:25,520
Hmm, Fingers are...

78
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:27,564
..this is "buṛēē aṅauṛi" (big finger)(thumb).

79
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:28,523
Hmm...hmm...

80
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:29,274
A "cunḍul aṅguṛi" (index finger).

81
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:29,941
Hmm...hmm...

82
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,150
This is "tālā aṅguṛi" (middle finger).

83
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:32,485
That's "bisi aṅguṛi" (thumb).

84
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:33,653
This is "kāni aṅaguṛi" (ring finger).

85
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:35,405
Alright then.

86
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:36,072
Yes.

87
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:38,741
This is how it is said in Ho.

88
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:40,827
Okay, after this,

89
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:42,537
from here to "lāīḥ" (stomach).

90
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:44,664
Coming down from the neck...

91
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:45,331
..coming down

92
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,167
So what is this called?

93
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:47,750
from here to here

94
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,419
The "kuēm" (chest) goes from here to there

95
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:50,295
"Kuēm"...

96
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:50,879
..called "kuēm"

97
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:51,462
Yes.

98
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:53,840
"Lēṅgā kuēm" (Left chest) on this side.

99
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,633
"Jōōma kuēm" (Right chest) is on this side.

100
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:57,760
Yes, from here to there

101
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,970
Yes, that's "lāīḥ" (stomach).

102
00:02:58,970 --> 00:02:59,679
"Lāīḥ".

103
00:02:59,679 --> 00:02:59,846
Yes

104
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:01,222
oh, from stomach till here.

105
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:01,890
The bone from stomach,

106
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,349
what is that called?

107
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:04,350
That is called "ḍuri jāṅg" (waist bone).

108
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:05,435
It is called "ḍuri jāṅg" (waist bone).

109
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:05,852
Yeah.

110
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,437
Which one is called "māẏāṅg" (waist) then?

111
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:08,813
Waist is behind.

112
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:09,606
From here...

113
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:12,358
..from here till here is called "māẏāṅg".

114
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:13,109
Till this bone.

115
00:03:13,109 --> 00:03:14,235
"Māẏāṅg". "Māẏāṅg".

116
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,528
From here till here.

117
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:17,572
What is below the waist called?

118
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:20,575
Talking of below the waist,

119
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:24,579
Until the "jaṅg" (thigh),

120
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:25,204
Hmm...

121
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:28,625
It is called "isēbuā" (thigh)

122
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:29,959
"Isēbuā". "Isēbuā".

123
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:31,377
Can you lift the leg and say,

124
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:32,712
which one is called "bulu" (thigh)?

125
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:34,172
"Bulu" (thigh)...

126
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:41,137
From this till this position...is called "bulu".

127
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:41,846
Yeah...

128
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:43,306
Lift the thigh a bit.

129
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:45,099
What is this called?

130
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:46,184
This is "mukui" (knee).

131
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:47,143
[It is] called "mukui".

132
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:49,646
Okay, from here to here?

133
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:50,480
[It] is called "Ra-kāṭāka" (lower leg).

134
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,522
From here to here is called "ra-kāṭāka".

135
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:52,357
[It] is called "Ra-kāṭāka".

136
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:52,857
Hmm...

137
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:54,859
Okay, from here to here?

138
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,111
This is called "iṇḍikē" (ankle).

139
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:57,737
"iṇḍikē" (ankle)?

140
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:58,237
Yeah.

141
00:03:58,237 --> 00:03:59,113
Alright.

142
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:01,491
Yeah, it is called "iṇḍikē".

143
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:03,660
From here to here is called "iṇḍikē".

144
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,328
Here is the anke, at the back.

145
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:06,621
Back...ankle...ankle...yeah...

146
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:07,622
Okay, the other foot?

147
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:09,207
The other part is "kulusukāṭā" (foot).

148
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:09,832
"Kulusukāṭā".

149
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:10,375
Hmm...

150
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:12,752
From here till here is foot...

151
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:13,252
Yeah...

152
00:04:13,252 --> 00:04:15,463
From here to here is "iṇḍikē".

153
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:17,340
Yeah...yeah...

154
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,384
So, how names are given

155
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:23,221
down here in leg..down in foot?

156
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:27,600
This toe is called "mārāṅg āṅguḷi" (big finger, big toe).

157
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,728
all fingers are like fingers in hand...

158
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:33,022
named based on fingers in hand.

159
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:33,564
Yeah...

160
00:04:33,564 --> 00:04:36,150
Okay, this is...then,

161
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,986
Below your foot,

162
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:38,778
Lift your leg...

163
00:04:38,778 --> 00:04:39,320
Yeah

164
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,406
This, below your foot—what is it called?

165
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:41,906
"Tālkā" (sole).

166
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:42,865
It is called "tālkā".

167
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:43,366
Hmm...

168
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:47,078
From here to here—what is it called?

169
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,162
"Dābi".

170
00:04:48,913 --> 00:04:50,415
(correcting self) "daẏā dābi" (back)..."daẏā dābi".

171
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:52,291
The area from here to here is...

172
00:04:52,291 --> 00:04:53,918
"Daẏā dābi"..."daẏā"..."daẏā"...

173
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:56,587
Okay, what is this called—from here to here?

174
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:57,380
"Rupi" (back).

175
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,172
It is called "rupi". Yeah.

176
00:04:58,172 --> 00:04:59,966
This is "jam pā rupi" (right back).

177
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:00,508
Yeah...

178
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:01,259
This is called..."liṅgā rupi" (right back).

179
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:02,677
"Liṅgā rupi". "Liṅgā rupi".

180
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:04,137
Okay.

181
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:06,222
Okay, tell below the waist.

182
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:09,142
What is this to this called in our Ho [language]?

183
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:11,436
This is called "lāṇḍika" (buttock).

184
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:12,270
This is called "lāṇḍika" (buttock).

185
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,105
Don't take me wrong...

186
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,190
as we understand, it is called "lāṇḍika".

187
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,734
Hmm...okay...okay...

188
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,902
And this is called...

189
00:05:19,902 --> 00:05:21,779
This is called "jumkē" (calf)...this.

190
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:25,033
Someone call [ankle] "iṇḍikē", and, some call "āndu kāṭā".

191
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:25,992
"Āndu kāṭāaka" (ankle).
